.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_ZEEMAN "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_zeeman (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_zeeman \- find the Zeeman potential for a 2D system.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_zeeman
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the Zeeman splitting contribution to a potential profile.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-B\fR [ \fB\-\-magneticfield\fR ] arg (=0)
Magnetic field along growth axis [T].
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or
\&'l', for electrons, heavy holes or light
holes respectively.
.TP
\fB\-\-spinup\fR
Spin direction is 'up'. Down\-spin
assumed if this flag is not used.
.TP
\fB\-\-Tl\fR arg (=1.8)
Temperature of crystal lattice [K]
.TP
\fB\-M\fR [ \fB\-\-material\fR ] arg (=cdmnte)
Material ID: Currently, only "cdmnte"
for Cd(1\-x)Mn(x)Te is supported
.TP
\fB\-\-bandedgepotentialfile\fR arg (=v_b.r) File containing baseline potential to be
added to Zeeman potential
.TP
\fB\-\-totalpotentialfile\fR arg (=v.r)
Filename to which the total potential is
written.
.TP
\fB\-\-zeemanpotentialfile\fR arg (=v_z.r)
Filename to which the Zeeman potential
is written.
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'v_b.r'    Baseline potential:
              Column 1: spatial location [m]
              Column 2: potential [J]

   'x.r'      Alloy composition:
              Column 1: Spatial location [m]
              Column 2: Alloy fraction (x)

.SS Output files:
   'v_z.r'    Zeeman potential:
   'v.r'      Total potential (v_b + v_z):
              Column 1: Spatial location [m]
              Column 2: Potential [J]
.SH EXAMPLES

Find the Zeeman potential for spin-up states in an 8 T magnetic field at 2 K:
    qwwad_ef_zeeman --spinup --magneticfield 8 --Tl 2

Find the Zeeman potential for spin-down states in a 40 T magnetic field at 100 K:
    qwwad_ef_zeeman --magneticfield 40 --Tl 100
